        "metadata": {
          "category": "stories",
          "minAge": 8,
          "maxAge": 14,
          "media": {
            "duration": 8717,
            "fileSize": 141025892
          },
          "author": "Frances Hodgson Burnett",
          "description": "A Yoto Original adaptation of the classic novel by Frances Hodgson Burnett. The perfect introduction to this enchanting tale for young listeners. Narrated by Sarah Slimani and brought to life with music, sound effects, and a full cast.   \n\nMary Lennox lived a very fortunate life in India. But after the loss of both of her parents, she's thrust into a new existence in rural Yorkshire to live with her reclusive uncle in a gloomy English manor.   \n\nAt first, lonely Mary finds herself surrounded by mystery and silence. But everything begins to change when she discovers a hidden, locked garden that has been left untended for years.   \n\nFollow along as Mary sets out on a quest to uncover the secrets of the locked garden. With the help of Dickon and her newfound cousin, Colin, Mary works to bring the garden back to life. But will the power of nature and the beauty of friendship help more than just the garden bloom?   \n\nA captivating story of friendship, resilience, and nature’s restorative possibilities.",
